DF-HRS-105 criterion 2 — the zero-hit LIKE fallback is a FALLBACK, not a replacement
===================================================================================
The acceptance criterion: "when the FTS5 search yields 0 hits but the RAW
(unsanitized) query term is present in the store's messages table, serve the
results from the LIKE arm instead. This must be a genuine fallback (only when
FTS returns empty), not a replacement for FTS5."

Three discriminating cases, driven through the Python consumer boundary
(`specs/python-interop.md` §4) exactly like probe_fidelity.py, plus the Rust
regression tests in `tests/hrs105_search_fidelity.rs`.

RUNNER (exact commands)
-----------------------
    # stage the probe under its importable name (.py.txt evidence convention)
    mkdir -p /tmp/hrs-df105
    cp docs/evidence/dogfood-20261017/transcript_archive.py.txt \
       /tmp/hrs-df105/transcript_archive.py
    cp docs/evidence/dogfood-20261017/probe_zero_hit_fallback.py.txt \
       /tmp/hrs-df105/probe_zero_hit_fallback.py

    # post-fix (HEAD 6295059 / 3f22a78)
    cd /home/kara/hermes-rs
    cargo build --bin hermes-rs-session-adapter
    python3 /tmp/hrs-df105/probe_zero_hit_fallback.py \
      --adapter /var/tmp/hermes-cargo-target/debug/hermes-rs-session-adapter \
      --db /tmp/hrs-df105/final-fb.db

    # pre-fix (revision 1093dfd, scratch tree built in search-fidelity.log RUNNER)
    python3 /tmp/hrs-df105/probe_zero_hit_fallback.py \
      --adapter /tmp/hrs-df105/prefix-target/debug/hermes-rs-session-adapter \
      --db /tmp/hrs-df105/fallback-prefix.db

POST-FIX — 4/4 as expected
--------------------------
case  query                     search  raw-LIKE  expected  verdict
  A   alpha!                        2         1         2  ok (fallback must NOT replace FTS5 (2 = FTS answers))
  B   ok!                           1         1         1  ok (fallback must fire (raw term present, FTS5 token differs))
  C   zzz-no-such-text-zzz          0         0         0  ok (honest zero stays zero)
  C   zzz/no-such/text              0         0         0  ok (honest zero stays zero)

FAILURES: 0

PRE-FIX (1093dfd) — CASE B fails, the fallback does not exist
-------------------------------------------------------------
case  query                     search  raw-LIKE  expected  verdict
  A   alpha!                        2         1         2  ok (fallback must NOT replace FTS5 (2 = FTS answers))
  B   ok!                           0         1         1  FAIL (fallback must fire (raw term present, FTS5 token differs))
  C   zzz-no-such-text-zzz          0         0         0  ok (honest zero stays zero)
  C   zzz/no-such/text              0         0         0  ok (honest zero stays zero)

FAILURES: 1
  ('B', 'ok!', 0, 1, 1, 1)

CASE A is the discriminating control in both directions: rows `case A alpha
marker row` and `case A alpha!beta marker row`, queried with `alpha!`. The
sanitized query is `alpha`, which the FTS5 arm answers with BOTH rows (2), while
the raw term `alpha!` is present in only one (raw-LIKE 1). A replacement-shaped
implementation answers 1; a genuine fallback answers 2. It answers 2 before and
after the fix — the fallback never runs on a query MATCH can answer.

CASE B is the fallback's own RED arm: `aok!x` indexes (unicode61) as the tokens
`aok` and `x`, so the sanitized query `ok` matches neither token, while the
literal `ok!` is in the row. Pre-fix: 0 hits. Post-fix: 1 hit.

